<%# What this site stores about a visitor and why (CCS-148). PLACEHOLDER WORDING until the University's privacy office approves it. %>
<% content_for :body_class, "page-help" %>
<% content_for :title, "Privacy and data on Collections Navigator — University of Melbourne" %>
<%= render NexusCcs::PageBreadcrumbsComponent.new(trail: [ [ "Privacy and data", nil ] ]) %>
<%= render NexusCcs::PageBannerComponent.new(title: "Privacy and data on Collections Navigator", description: "What this site stores about you, why, for how long, and how to have it removed.") %>
<main class="help-main-content help-main-content--topic" id="main-content">
<div class="help-layout">
<nav class="jump-nav" aria-labelledby="jump-nav-title" data-controller="jump-nav">
  <div class="jump-nav__container">
    <p class="jump-nav__title" id="jump-nav-title">On this page</p>
    <ul class="jump-nav__list">
      <li class="jump-nav__item"><a class="jump-nav__link" data-jump-nav-target="link" href="#what-we-store">What this site stores</a></li>
      <li class="jump-nav__item"><a class="jump-nav__link" data-jump-nav-target="link" href="#cookies">Cookies</a></li>
      <li class="jump-nav__item"><a class="jump-nav__link" data-jump-nav-target="link" href="#requests">Requests for access</a></li>
      <li class="jump-nav__item"><a class="jump-nav__link" data-jump-nav-target="link" href="#your-choices">Your choices</a></li>
      <li class="jump-nav__item"><a class="jump-nav__link" data-jump-nav-target="link" href="#more-information">More information</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</nav>
<div class="help-layout__content">
<div class="placeholder-notice" role="note" id="placeholder-notice">
  <p><strong>Placeholder wording, not yet approved.</strong> The University's privacy office must approve this notice, including how long data is kept and the legal basis, before it is relied on. It describes what the site does today.</p>
</div>

<section class="help-section" id="what-we-store" aria-labelledby="h-what-we-store">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-what-we-store">What this site stores</h2>
    <p class="help-section__description">You do not sign in. The site knows you only by a cookie in your browser.</p>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Searching and reading records</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">The words and filters of the searches you make are stored by the site, and the cookie in your browser lists which are yours, so you can see your search history and go back to them. The site does not ask who you are to search or read records. <span data-placeholder>[Placeholder: how long old searches are kept.]</span></p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Saved records, lists and saved searches</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">When you save a record, make a list or save a search, the site keeps it against a visitor number, linked to your browser by the cookie. It holds no name or email address. If you clear your cookies, you lose the way back to it. <span data-placeholder>[Placeholder: how long unused saved items are kept before they are removed.]</span></p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Sharing a list by link</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">If you choose to share a list, the site makes a long random link. Anyone who has the link can see the list's name, description and records, and copy it to their own lists. The page does not say who made it, is not listed on the site and is kept out of search engines, but anyone you give the link to can pass it on. You can stop sharing or make a new link at any time, and deleting the list or using Delete my data ends the link at once. Records shown in a shared page or an embedded card follow the same rules as the rest of the site: images that are withheld or sensitive are not shown. <span data-placeholder>[Placeholder: wording to be approved by the University's privacy office.]</span></p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Choices about sensitive records</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">When you choose to view or not view the images of a record that carries a sensitive-content notice, your choice is kept in the cookie only.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Recently viewed records</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">The record pages list the last records you opened, so you can go back to them. Only their numbers are kept, in the cookie, and nobody else can see the list.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Records of visits</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">Like most web sites, the servers that run this site keep a log of requests, which includes addresses, the page asked for and the time. It is used to run and protect the site. <span data-placeholder>[Placeholder: who can see the logs, where they are held and for how long. The development team to confirm.]</span></p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item" id="view-counts">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Which records are most viewed</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">To show "trending" records on the home page and the Discover page, the site counts, for each record and each day, how many times the record page was opened by a web browser. Only the record's number, the day and the count are stored. The site does not store who looked: no cookie, visitor number, session, address or browser details go with a count, so nothing in the counts can be linked to you, and Delete my data has nothing of this kind to remove. Visits by search engines, scrapers and other programs, and visits to records with withheld or sensitive images, are not counted. Counts older than about five weeks are removed. <span data-placeholder>[Placeholder: the University to confirm the retention period.]</span></p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Other web sites</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">The pages of this site load their fonts, scripts and styles from the site itself, not from other companies. Some links take you to other University of Melbourne web sites, which have their own notices.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="help-section" id="cookies" aria-labelledby="h-cookies">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-cookies">Cookies</h2>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text"><%= t("nexus_ccs.cookie_notice.privacy.intro") %> <%= t("nexus_ccs.cookie_notice.privacy.none_optional") %> Your browser also keeps, for the visit only, which filters you had open. <span data-placeholder>[Placeholder: the University to confirm that these cookies need no consent banner, and whether any University-wide analytics will be added.]</span></p>
    </li>
    <% CookieNotice.essential.each do |cookie| %>
      <li class="help-section__item">
        <h3 class="help-section__subheading"><code><%= cookie.name %></code></h3>
        <p class="help-section__text"><%= t("nexus_ccs.cookie_notice.cookies.#{cookie.key}.purpose") %> <strong><%= t("nexus_ccs.cookie_notice.privacy.lifetime") %>:</strong> <%= t("nexus_ccs.cookie_notice.cookies.#{cookie.key}.lifetime") %>. <strong><%= t("nexus_ccs.cookie_notice.privacy.essential") %></strong> for the site to work.</p>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="help-section" id="requests" aria-labelledby="h-requests">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-requests">Requests for access</h2>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text">If you ask for access to a record, the site stores your name, email address, organisation, the reason you give and the record, so that the collection team can answer you. This is a record the University must be able to act on and keep, so it is <strong>not</strong> removed by the Delete my data action below. To have a request corrected or removed, contact the collection team through <a href="<%= help_path(anchor: "contact-us") %>">Contact Us</a>. <span data-placeholder>[Placeholder: how long requests are kept, and who at the University may see them.]</span></p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="help-section" id="your-choices" aria-labelledby="h-your-choices">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-your-choices">Your choices</h2>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <% if Rails.configuration.x.saved_records %>
        <p class="help-section__text">You can remove everything the site holds against your browser (saved records, lists, saved searches, search history and your choices about sensitive records) at any time. Go to <a href="<%= my_data_path %>">Delete my data</a>.</p>
      <% else %>
        <p class="help-section__text">You can clear your search history from the search history page, or clear your cookies in your browser's settings.</p>
      <% end %>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text">To ask what the University holds about you, or to correct it, use <a href="<%= help_path(anchor: "contact-us") %>">Contact Us</a>.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="help-section" id="more-information" aria-labelledby="h-more-information">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-more-information">More information</h2>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text">The University's privacy notice and its privacy obligations are on the <a href="https://about.unimelb.edu.au/strategy/governance/compliance-obligations/privacy">University of Melbourne privacy page</a>. That page, not this one, is the University's statement of its obligations.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
</div>
</div>
</main>
